From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs8550-ayn-thor: set gamepad axis range

The Thor sticks reach approximately 1024 counts, while the shared rsinput
driver defaults to a range of 0x580 (1408).  Advertising the larger range
causes userspace to see only about 73 percent deflection, which can leave
games below their run threshold.

Use the rsinput driver's board-specific axis-range property for Thor.  Keep
the shared default unchanged for other AYN devices that use the same driver.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -157,6 +157,10 @@ multi-ledl4 {
 	};
 };
 
+&gamepad {
+	axis-range = <1024>;
+};
+
 &display_panel {
 	compatible = "chipone,icna3520";
 
